parts.text:
Now let me update the Tokens struct and related functions. I'll use `pathland_core::tokens::TokenValue`. Let me modify:

1. The `Tokens` struct (lines ~572-611):
```rust
struct Tokens {
    base: BTreeMap<String, (u8, TokenValue)>,
    dark: BTreeMap<String, (u8, TokenValue)>,
}
```
2. `set`:
```rust
fn set(&mut self, path: &str, value_type: u8, value: TokenValue) { ... }
```
3. `css()`: iterate, `token_css_value(path, *vt, value)`.
4. `token_css_value(path, value_type, value: &TokenValue) -> String`:
```rust
fn token_css_value(path: &str, value_type: u8, value: &TokenValue) -> String {
    match value {
        TokenValue::Str(s) => format!("'{}'", s.replace('\\', "\\\\").replace('\'', "\\'")),
        _ => {
            let v = value.to_bits().unwrap_or(0);
            match value_type {
                value_type::COLOR => rgba(v),
                value_type::F32 => {
                    let v = f32::from_bits(v);
                    if is_length_token(path) { format!("{v}px") } else { format!("{v}") }
                }
                value_type::I32 => format!("{}", v as i32),
                value_type::U32 => format!("{}", v),
                value_type::U8 => format!("{}", v & 0xFF),
                _ => format!("{}", v),
            }
        }
    }
}
```
Hmm — but `to_bits()` for F32 returns the f32 bits; then I reinterpret. For Color it returns argb. OK. Actually simpler: match on TokenValue directly:
```rust
match value {
    Str(s) => quote,
    Color(c) => rgba(*c),
    F32(f) => { if is_length_token(path) { format!("{f}px") } else { format!("{f}") } },
    I32(i) => format!("{i}"),
    U32(u) => format!("{u}"),
    U8(u) => format!("{u}"),
}
```
This is cleaner and doesn't need value_type. Let me rewrite `token_css_value` to take `&TokenValue`. But there's a subtlety: the F32 length-px check needs the path. Keep path param.

5. `decode`: 
```rust
if op.command() == style::SET_DESIGN_TOKEN {
    if let Some(path) = strings_str(strings, op.a()) {
        let vt = (op.b() & 0xFF) as u8;
        let value = if vt == value_type::STRING {
            strings_str(strings, op.c()).map(TokenValue::Str).unwrap_or(TokenValue::U32(0))
        } else {
            TokenValue::from_wire(vt, op.c()).unwrap_or(TokenValue::U32(op.c()))
        };
