- color.success/warning/danger/info: greens/yellows/reds... (Tier 2; add basic)
- font.body.size: 16.0 / weight 400.0 / family "Inter, sans-serif" (Str)
- space.base: 4.0
- radius.xs/sm/md/lg/xl: 2/6/6/8/12 (px as f32), full → special (huge)? GTK border-radius in px. full → 9999.
- border.width.thin: 1.0
- control.*: background 0xFFFFFFFF, foreground 0xFF111827, border 0xFFD1D5DB, border.width 1.0, radius 6.0, height 36.0, padding.horizontal 12.0, padding.vertical 6.0, font.size 14.0, font.weight 600.0, accent 0xFF2563EB. dark variants.

GTK-native defaults via `gtk::StyleContext::lookup_color`:
- A `GtkTheme` module in lib.rs (or tokens.rs in render-gtk) that resolves named colors:
  - color.background → "theme_bg_color"
  - color.surface → "theme_base_color"
  - color.text.primary → "theme_fg_color"
  - color.text.secondary → "theme_unfocused_fg_color"
  - color.border → "borders"
  - color.accent / color.primary → "theme_selected_bg_color"
  - color.text.onPrimary → "theme_selected_fg_color"
  - color.success → "success_color", color.warning → "warning_color", color.danger → "error_color"

